[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3110781822","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108916#issuecomment-3110781822","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108916","id":3110781822,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65asN-","user":{"login":"JonathanHaws","id":108207472,"node_id":"U_kgDOBnMdcA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108207472?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws","html_url":"https://github.com/JonathanHaws","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-23T22:42:00Z","updated_at":"2025-07-23T22:42:56Z","body":"Engine.time_scale doesn't effect audio at all I think. Which is a good thing as games can add brief pauses for impact without having to set process mode to always on playback nodes. Because 'get_tree().paused = true' does stop playback. \r\n\r\nThe original game I found the bug in uses 3d navigation for pathfinding. I use  `get_next_path_position()`  on each agent and then apply velocity to the agent's body. Which the navigation function is not delta dependent to my knowledge. So ultimately the bug came back to move_and_slide there anyways \r\n\r\nI think this code probably fixes the majority of bugs caused by setting time_scale to 0 most people will encounter. But probably is a good idea to keep an eye out for other functions that should be skipped when time_scale is 0. Or atleast throw a warning of unpredictable behavior \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3110781822/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3111147102","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108916#issuecomment-3111147102","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108916","id":3111147102,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65cFZe","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-23T23:19:31Z","updated_at":"2025-07-23T23:19:31Z","body":"Added a check that removes the ability to set negative values to `Engine.time_scale`.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3111147102/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3112877850","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108916#issuecomment-3112877850","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108916","id":3112877850,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65ir8a","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-24T10:11:31Z","updated_at":"2025-07-24T10:11:31Z","body":"> `JoltPhysicsServer3D::step` does more than just step the simulation, and since you're not doing an early return in `PhysicsServer3D::flush_queries` (which you arguably shouldn't) you may or may not end up with some strange issues now that one will not always be followed by the other.\r\n\r\nThinking about this some more, you would almost certainly be changing the behavior of `_integrate_forces` with this change, as it gets called as part of `PhysicsServer3D::flush_queries` for all active bodies, but that list is wiped and re-populated on every `PhysicsServer3D::step`, so you would most likely no longer be calling `_integrate_forces` while time scale is 0.\r\n\r\nThis would apply to Godot Physics as well.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3112877850/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3112934302","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108916#issuecomment-3112934302","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108916","id":3112934302,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65i5ue","user":{"login":"JonathanHaws","id":108207472,"node_id":"U_kgDOBnMdcA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108207472?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws","html_url":"https://github.com/JonathanHaws","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-24T10:30:04Z","updated_at":"2025-07-24T10:30:04Z","body":"> Anyway, I would ask that you leave `JoltPhysicsServer3D` out of this change for now, if you just need to get the Godot Physics part merged. I've been careful not to divide by a zero timestep in that module, so everything should work fine with a time scale of 0 when using Jolt.\r\n\r\nDid a quick verification and indeed Jolt does not have this issue. \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/17ad54dc-0a9f-4224-b573-c58fcb7e124b\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3112934302/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3113600164","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108916#issuecomment-3113600164","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108916","id":3113600164,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65lcSk","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-24T14:02:32Z","updated_at":"2025-07-24T14:02:32Z","body":"Closing as this PR was implementing a very naive approach. I think Godot Physics 2D/3D should follow the same 0 checks as Jolt does.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3113600164/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]